      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 50 mg of amlodipine once daily is five times the maximum recommended daily dose, which is 10 mg. Doses above 10 mg can cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. The usual starting dose is 2.5 to 5 mg daily, and the usual maximum is 10 mg.\n\nThis may be a typo, such as 5 mg written as 50 mg. Please confirm the intended dose with the prescribing physician before anything is entered. If the prescriber confirms 50 mg is intended, they will need to enter the order themselves with clinical documentation.\n\nI can enter the order once a licensed prescriber confirms the dose. Also, since you are not a clinician, the prescriber should be the one to place or sign off on this order."
      }
